<title>USA: TABLE - Phar-Mor Inc Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Phar-Mor Inc Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>YOUNGSTOWN, Ohio 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.03     loss	 $0.22</p>
<p> Net profit		   413     loss	 2,684</p>
<p> Revs		     255,301		  264,798</p>
<p>			    YEAR</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.19   profit	 $0.27</p>
<p> Net loss		   2,281   profit	 3,330</p>
<p> Revs		   1,074,828		1,056,252</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Fiscal year ended June 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Fiscal year results on pro forma basis. Phar-Mor emerged from Chapter 11 bankruptcy in Sept, 1995. Consequently the company has applied reorganization and fresh-start reporting adjustments to balance sheet as of Sept, 1995.</p>
<p>Pro forma info includes all retroactive adjustments for fresh start accounting, elimination of non-recurring reorganization items and adjusted interest expense to give effect to new debt of reorganized company.</p>
<p>Fiscal 1997 results include about $3.1 million in expenses associated with proposed business combination with ShopKo Stores.</p>
